            {
              "id": "neetprep_physics_q450830",
              "type": "mcq",
              "originalOrder": 2,
              "topic": "Magnetic Flux",
              "subtopic": "Magnetic Flux",
              "sub_category": "Magnetic Flux",
              "chapter": "Electromagnetic Induction",
              "exam_name": "NCERT Based",
              "question": "A loop, made of straight edges has six corners at <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(A(0,0,0), B(L, 0,0), C(L,L,0), D(0,L,0), E(0,L,L)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(F(0,0,L).\\)</span>&nbsp;A magnetic field&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(B=B_0(\\hat{i}+\\hat{k})~\\text{T}\\)</span>&nbsp;is present in the region. The flux passing through the loop <span class=\"math-tex\">\\(ABCDEFA\\)</span> (in that order) is:\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"min-width: 300px;\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(( B_0 L^2 )~\\text{Wb} \\)</span></td><td>2.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((2 B_0 L^2 )~\\text{Wb} \\)</span></td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(( \\sqrt{2} B_0 L^2 )~\\text{Wb} \\)</span></td><td>4.</td><td><span class=\"math-tex\">\\((4 B_0 L^2) ~\\text{Wb} \\)</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\r\n&nbsp;",
              "options": [
                "(1)",
                "(2)",
                "(3)",
                "(4)"
              ],
              "correct": 1,
              "explanation": "Hint:\\(\\phi_m=\\vec{B} \\cdot \\vec{A}\\)\n\nStep: Find theflux passing through the loop\\(ABCDEFA\\)\nThe loop \\(ABCDA\\) lies in the\\((x\\text-y)\\) plane whose area vector \n\\(\\vec{A}_1=L^2 \\widehat{k},\\) whereas the loop \\(ADEFA\\) lies in the\n\\((y\\text-z)\\) plane whose area vector\\(\\vec{A}_2=L^2 \\hat{i}.\\)\nand the magnetic flux is given by;\n\\(\\phi_m=\\vec{B} \\cdot \\vec{A}\\)\n\\(\\vec{A}=\\vec{A}_1+\\vec{A}_2=\\left(L^2 \\widehat{k}+L^2 \\hat{i}\\right)\\)\nAnd \\(\\vec{B}=B_0(\\hat{i}+\\widehat{k})\\)\nSubstitute the given values we get;\nNow, \\(\\phi_m=\\vec{B} \\cdot \\vec{A}=B_0(\\hat{i}+\\widehat{k}) \\cdot\\left(L^2\n\\widehat{k}+L^2 \\hat{i}\\right)\\)\n\\(\\Rightarrow \\phi_m=(2 B_0 L^2)~\\text{Wb} \\)\nHence, option (2) is the correct answer.<div style=\"margin-top:1.25rem; padding:0.85rem 1rem; background:var(--bg-secondary); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:8px;\"><div style=\"display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; margin-bottom:0.6rem; font-weight:600; font-size:0.88rem;\"><span>📊 Student Attempt Analytics</span><span style=\"padding:2px 8px; border-radius:12px; font-size:0.75rem; font-weight:700; background:rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.15); color:#d97706;\">🟡 Medium · 46% Got This Correct</span></div><div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:0.5rem; text-align:center; font-size:0.82rem;\"><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(1)</div><div style=\"font-weight:700; margin-top:2px;\">12%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:rgba(34,197,94,0.12); border:1.5px solid #22c55e;\"><div style=\"color:#16a34a; font-weight:700;\">(2) ✓</div><div style=\"font-weight:800; color:#16a34a; margin-top:2px;\">47%</div></div><div style=\"padding:0.4rem; border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg-primary); border:1px solid var(--border);\"><div>(3)</div