              "question": "A circular coil expands radially in a region of magnetic field and no electromotive force is produced in the coil. This can be because:\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"min-width: 300px;\"><tbody><tr><td>(a)</td><td>the magnetic field is constant.</td></tr><tr><td>(b)</td><td>the magnetic field is in the same plane as the circular coil and it may or may not vary.</td></tr><tr><td>(c)</td><td>the magnetic field has a perpendicular (to the plane of the coil) component whose magnitude is decreasing suitably.</td></tr><tr><td>(d)</td><td>there is a constant magnetic field in the perpendicular (to the plane of the coil) direction.</td></tr></tbody></table>\r\nChoose the correct option:\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"min-width: 300px;\"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>(a), (c)</td><td>2.</td><td>(a), (b), (c)</td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td>(b), (c)</td><td>4.</td><td>(c), (d)</td></tr></tbody></table>",
              "options": [
                "(1)",
                "(2)",
                "(3)",
                "(4)"
